    "body": "**Measured trade-off / no recommended shipping PR. Three authorized comparisons are permanently closed.**\r\n\r\nThe legacy managed Decrypt MemoryStream capacity experiment consistently reduces large partial-block AppDomain-inclusive managed allocation about 40%. SHA256 64 KiB+1 also improves time 34-36% in every comparison. These benefits are real and retained; the no-gain/inconclusive campaign disposition does not mean zero allocation improvement.\r\n\r\nHowever, small/aligned controls and large latency reversals prevent the combined acceptance gate from passing. SHA512 1 MiB+1 has time changes -9.19%, -16.36%, then **+57.11%**, giving **+8.91% aggregate time** despite 39.95% lower allocation. Its final candidate CV is 18.80%; no cause is established and that result is not discarded as noise. SHA256 small aggregates are 4-16% slower, empty inputs increase B/op, and aligned large controls show no structural allocation saving. No fourth run or tuning outside the budget.\r\n\r\n[Immutable complete matrix, every raw result, exact candidate patch, runnable project, actual validation commands and limitations](https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/blob/2ee3d1d7df2d67e6e679110eccb36c065c5937dd/F016/README.md)\r\n\r\n| Shape | Original us | Capacity us | Time change | Original B/op | Capacity B/op | Allocation change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Aes256Sha256_P0 | 104.204 | 109.460 | 5.04% | 2651.0 | 2672.7 | 0.82% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P15 | 104.596 | 110.245 | 5.40% | 2966.7 | 2700.0 | -8.99% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P16 | 104.965 | 109.482 | 4.30% | 2963.0 | 2716.7 | -8.31% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P17 | 104.826 | 110.496 | 5.41% | 2982.3 | 2735.0 | -8.29% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P191 | 104.950 | 114.372 | 8.98% | 3319.7 | 3229.3 | -2.72% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P192 | 104.561 | 121.588 | 16.29% | 3319.0 | 3244.3 | -2.25% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P193 | 104.535 | 115.428 | 10.42% | 3335.0 | 3263.0 | -2.16% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P255 | 105.571 | 116.086 | 9.96% | 3447.0 | 3423.0 | -0.70% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P256 | 104.753 | 116.013 | 10.75% | 3448.0 | 3438.7 | -0.27% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P257 | 104.708 | 115.519 | 10.32% | 4001.3 | 3457.0 | -13.60% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P1024 | 105.998 | 117.796 | 11.13% | 5756.7 | 5748.7 | -0.14% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P1025 | 108.049 | 116.806 | 8.10% | 7851.7 | 5764.7 | -26.58% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P65536 | 184.396 | 193.345 | 4.85% | 199539.7 | 199558.3 | 0.01% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P65537 | 282.168 | 182.555 | -35.30% | 330896.3 | 199559.7 | -39.69% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P1048576 | 1668.726 | 1706.095 | 2.24% | 3153834.3 | 3153527.0 | -0.01% |\n| Aes256Sha256_P1048577 | 1644.672 | 1587.847 | -3.46% | 5250548.0 | 3153523.3 | -39.94% |\n| Aes256Sha512_P0 | 110.149 | 109.752 | -0.36% | 3053.7 | 3070.0 | 0.53% |\n| Aes256Sha512_P1024 | 113.478 | 112.380 | -0.97% | 6160.0 | 6151.7 | -0.14% |\n| Aes256Sha512_P1025 | 116.072 | 112.705 | -2.90% | 8253.3 | 6167.7 | -25.27% |\n| Aes256Sha512_P1048576 | 3084.800 | 3167.226 | 2.67% | 3153359.0 | 3153360.0 | 0.00% |\n| Aes256Sha512_P1048577 | 3326.249 | 3622.659 | 8.91% | 5250895.7 | 3153167.0 | -39.95% |\r\n\r\nThe candidate changes only the legacy Decrypt constructor to `new MemoryStream(capacity: macOffset - ciphertextOffset)`. This is a padded-ciphertext upper bound, **not exact plaintext length**. Encrypt, F015's separate proposal, modern NET, APIs and all surrounding statements remain untouched. Both temporary source files are restored; the independent source branch stays at baseline `37e809ead5824bc753a1c3d56f11615bdb1296c5`. The exact two-file +37/-1 experiment and preservation test remain in the capsule's applicable candidate.patch. No new source commit, optimization PR or recommended merge.\r\n\r\nActual public managed configuration/descriptor/Secret.Random/factory creates the backend; strict Moq only supplies public IKey Descriptor metadata outside timing. Real public Encrypt produces a fixed payload outside timing. Actual public IAuthenticatedEncryptor.Decrypt is timed and returns its actual byte array. No per-call RNG is claimed for Decrypt; no copied backend/private invocation/new visibility or replacement algorithm/entropy. Nonzero offsets, exact outputs, whole input preservation and default/empty-AAD contracts are exercised through the real owners.\r\n\r\nActual net472/x64 executable/real net462 owner, installed Framework4.8 corelib4.8.10008, concurrent workstation GC; not the modern product. Untimed net12 compatibility executes actual netstandard2.0. Six21-case profiles:126 reports,1008 raw actual/952 retained/56 upper-filtered,378 warmups/2256 overheads. The same candidate is compared O/C,C/O,O/C. All252 settings point records remain Normal/Normal/affinity65535 via settings-preserving executor. Shared Hyper-V VM, not isolated; no power/priority/affinity changes or unrelated process termination.\r\n\r\nActual all3 product TFMs build; both original/candidate owning suites pass40net12+24net472 rows each,0failed/skipped. `Decrypt_BlockAndStreamBoundaries_PreservesPayloadAndInputs` individually passes all9 rows on both targets and both roles:36 executions. Scoped formatter changes0of2; enabled APICompat pack actually passes and all3packed owner bytes match frozen products; released baseline version unset. Relocated standalone Prepare builds pass for original and candidate,91-file images; **no native execution or new timing**.\r\n\r\nIndependent live/copied audits pass:406frozen files rehashed,28source snapshots,20PE/PDB records/110selected documents,504real roundtrip records,12contracts and128owning TRX rows. Paired91-file Framework and77-file compatibility images differ only owner DLL/PDB. Selected witnesses are not complete compiler provenance. Portable audit cannot reopen omitted binaries/binlogs/packages; exact omission hashes remain.\r\n\r\nBDN0.13 Framework allocation is AppDomain-inclusive forced-GC accounting, not isolated stream/native/working-set bytes. No production-frequency/default-app/whole-current-default SDK/modern-path throughput claim, no universal reduction, and no claim all original calls grow. Captured default49147673007a4b1d676694e2c5f85b83ad76c36f19-file triples differ only Versions.props. Merged dotnet/aspnetcore#70146 is modern-path work, not this legacy capacity seam; no upstream measurements are reused. The actual bounded open-PR search finds dotnet/aspnetcore#66438 cross-version tests.\r\n\n\nUnchanged independent source branch: https://github.com/jaslawinMs/aspnetcore/tree/autoperf/F016-managed-decryption-capacity\n\r\n",
